---
title: "client_authority_update (Sui Whitepaper: Relayer Protocol)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_init_list: initialize sync list with target TxCert
    q_init_list --> q_consider_last: consider last TxCert in sync list

    q_consider_last --> q_extract_inputs: extract Tx from TxCert, derive inputs(Tx)
    q_extract_inputs --> q_check_input: for each input object ObjRef

    q_check_input --> q_lookup_parent: find Tx that generated or mutated object (via Sync_v)
    q_lookup_parent --> q_check_in_B: check if parent cert exists in lagging authority B

    q_check_in_B --> q_next_input: certificate already in B
    q_check_in_B --> q_add_to_list: certificate not in B, read from Ct_v and add to sync list

    q_add_to_list --> q_consider_last: process newly added certificate

    q_next_input --> q_check_input: more input objects remaining
    q_next_input --> q_check_more_certs: all inputs for this cert checked

    q_check_more_certs --> q_consider_last: more certificates in sync list need processing
    q_check_more_certs --> q_sort: no more certificates to add

    q_sort --> q_submit: sort certificates in causal order
    q_submit --> [*]: submit sorted certificates to lagging authority B

    note right of q_check_in_B
        INV-001: Relayer operation is keyless and untrusted for integrity
        INV-002: Multiple relayers can operate independently and concurrently
        INV-003: Algorithm finds smallest set of certificates needed to sync
        INV-004: Causal ordering ensures authority processes certificates in valid order
    end note
